{
    "background_story": "Langston was a jazz musician who found his inspiration in the vibrant city of Newport, Rhode Island. Growing up in the historic district, he was surrounded by the sounds of the sea and the rhythms of the city's rich musical heritage. Langston's love affair with jazz began at the famous Newport Jazz Festival, where he was mesmerized by the performances of legendary musicians. He spent countless hours practicing his saxophone on the scenic coastal drives, letting the ocean breeze guide his improvisations. As he honed his craft, Langston became a staple of the Newport music scene, playing to packed houses at local clubs and eventually, the festival that had first sparked his passion. His soulful melodies captured the essence of the city, earning him the nickname 'The Newport Crooner'. Langston's music remained forever tied to the charm and beauty of his beloved Newport.",
